US-005 is implemented and verified.

**Changes**
- `frontend/src/core/apiClient.js` — on a 401 (outside the public `/api/auth/local*` endpoints) the response interceptor now calls `clearStoredSession()` instead of four manual `removeItem`s, then emits `window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent(AUTH_EXPIRED_EVENT))`. `AUTH_EXPIRED_EVENT = "auth:expired"` is exported so the provider and tests share the name.
- `frontend/src/context/AuthContext.js` — new `useEffect` registering an `auth:expired` listener that does `setUser(null)`, with `removeEventListener` cleanup. With `user` null, the existing `ProtectedRoute` in `App.js:45` redirects to `/login`; no change needed there.
- `frontend/src/context/__tests__/AuthContext.expired.test.jsx` (new, 5 cases) — 401 clears localStorage and fires the event; 401 from the login endpoint does not; 500 leaves the session alone; `AuthProvider` ends with `user` null after a 401; listener is removed on unmount. It drives the real `api` instance with a per-request axios `adapter`, so no network or mock library is involved.

**Quality gates** (all from `frontend/`)
- `npm run typecheck` — passes
- `npx eslint 'src/**/*.{js,jsx}'` — passes
- `CI=true npx react-scripts test --watchAll=false` — 11 suites / 56 tests pass

`progress.md` has the US-005 entry plus two new Codebase Patterns (the `auth:expired` contract and the axios-adapter technique for testing interceptors). No commits were made.

